# No HTML outside demos

This repo is **host-agnostic**: not tied to HTML, the DOM, or any graphic
design system. Library code under `src/<package>/` (everything except
`demo/`, `*.stories.tsx`, and docs) must not emit HTML elements or
design-specific chrome.

## Forbidden in library code

- Intrinsic JSX: `<div>`, `<span>`, `<button>`, `<input>`, `<h1>`–`<h6>`,
  `<p>`, `<section>`, `<label>`, `<pre>`, … (any lowercase DOM tag)
- Inline visual styling meant as product UI (`style={{ … }}` for layout,
  color, typography) on library-owned elements
- Hardcoded design-system widgets (icons, themed titles, scrolled shells)

`React.Fragment` (`<>…</>`), composition of host-provided `ReactNode`, and
calling host **render props** are fine.

## Required pattern

Inject chrome via **render props / HOC args** (same seam as `SectionHOC`,
`Side`, `AddFormItem`, …):

```typescript
// ✅ Library — structure + callbacks only
return render({ title, onSelect, search, setSearch });

// ✅ Demo / host — owns HTML
render: ({ title, onSelect }) => (
  <button type="button" onClick={onSelect}>{title}</button>
);
```

```typescript
// ❌ Library — ships HTML/design
return (
  <button type="button" onClick={onSelect} style={{ padding: 8 }}>
    {title}
  </button>
);
```

## Where HTML is allowed

| Path | OK? |
|---|---|
| `src/<pkg>/demo/**` | Yes |
| `src/<pkg>/*.stories.tsx` | Yes (Storybook entry) |
| `src/<pkg>/**` library modules | **No** |
| `src/main.tsx` | App stub only — not a package API |

If a school source file mixes logic + JSS/HTML, port the **logic** into the
library and leave the chrome in the demo (or a host render-prop).
